<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sahle Selassie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1795">1795</a>–<a href="/years/1847">1847</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sahle Selassie was ruler of Shewa in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> from 1813 to 1847, the first of his line to take the title negus, king. He expanded Shewa into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oromo">Oromo</a> lands, combined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Christian kingship with alliances with Muslim and Oromo neighbours, and received British and French missions. He was the grandfather of the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sahle-selassie.jpg" alt="Sahle Selassie" width="320" height="301" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Sahla_Sellase_colour.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
